{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:40:37.602080784Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-c3342455","body":"Fix inconsistent SUB_ADULT_FEEDING_WEIGHT constant: 0.65 in crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:148 vs 0.67 in crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:16. These two private constants serve the same conceptual role (sub-adult feeding demand relative to adults) but disagree on the value. biology.rs uses it in AnimalState::feeding_units() and add_reserve_by_feeding_units(), while shrimp.rs uses it in the actual daily feeding/routing/condition code. Consolidate to a single shared constant (or single source of truth) to prevent silent divergence in feeding weight calculations between the two modules.","dedup_key":"645ad12391518d47f38bfbd71b6a5fc2eb5ca1e85e5a919250a265710dacbc7f","run_id":"run-20260328125548","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":15,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:40:37.610577633Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7041f312","body":"Fix failing test trim_plants_is_closed_system_via_helpers in crates/tank_core/tests/budget_helpers.rs:242-267. Two issues: (1) Line 253 calls assert_n_conserved() but TrimPlantsAndRemove intentionally exports biomass from the tank — this is no longer a closed-system operation, so the nitrogen conservation assertion is incorrect for the renamed action semantics. (2) Line 259 looks up budget label \"action:trim_plants\" but the action was renamed to TrimPlantsAndRemove with budget label \"action:trim_plants_and_remove\" (engine.rs:791), so the lookup always returns None and the test would panic at the .expect() even if the conservation check passed.","dedup_key":"927b8fe43579afa16a1c17500328412c35f660a22c0b58735454f559e956de74","run_id":"run-20260328125548","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":16,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:40:37.618987217Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-8bfaab0f","body":"Fix incorrect reserve fraction in RemoveShrimp action at crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:684. The code computes `removed_frac = count.min(total) / total` where `total = state.animal.total_count()` (adults + sub-adults + juveniles) but `count` is the number of adults to remove. This dilutes the reserve fraction — removing 5 adults from a population of 5 adults + 10 juveniles only removes 5/15 = 33% of adult reserve instead of 100%. The denominator should be `state.animal.adult.count` to correctly export the proportional adult reserve.","dedup_key":"2d517dbdba0222f0cc5ff8818e5dd7c44775e4e6b989c3ae560d9b489e9d7b6d","run_id":"run-20260328125548","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":17,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:40:37.627445253Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-fa860636","body":"Remove dead code in crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs: the methods feeding_units() (line 441), add_reserve_by_feeding_units() (line 477), try_spend_reserve_g() (line 497), and transfer_dead_reserve_g() (line 517) have zero call sites across the entire codebase. They were likely intended as refactoring targets but the shrimp.rs code does the same operations inline with its own (different) constant values. Either wire these methods into the actual simulation code or remove them to avoid confusion with the divergent constants.","dedup_key":"2ed4dedbb7f76431f8193a243f1e2d20f13f74001b3e5e0509d0b86b632226e6","run_id":"run-20260328125548","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":18,"timestamp":"2026-03-28T13:40:37.635918537Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-ae828701","body":"`/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/budget_tracking.rs:287`, `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/budget_tracking.rs:303`, and `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/tests/budget_tracking.rs:441` hard-code the current animal cohort names (`adult`, `sub_adult`, `juvenile`) and only treat flat `animal.*_count` names as future fields. A new nested cohort following the current schema, such as `animal.larvae.count` or `animal.larvae.reserve_g`, would no longer be auto-discovered by the structural coverage test, so the budget component arrays could drift out of sync without this guard failing.","dedup_key":"f907167f76890d52c426f5d5e7b568700a020973faecae4d952950a7421d03bf","run_id":"run-20260328125548","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
